scope: Network+ final brief + answer review, HEAD 166880000, after SIX rounds and FIVE blocks. Round 6 verdict verbatim: NANCY: PASS. She verified independently from scratch rather than re-reading my claims: replicated 0/20 false failures on the committed render suite; used the sanctioned NETFINAL_RENDER_PAGE override to serve a scratch copy with the clock guard reverted and got 6/6 detection with an observed worst-rise of 2s against a 1s tolerance; ran 2 baseline + 2 detection passes at NETFINAL_RENDER_THROTTLE=4 (2/2 green, 2/2 caught); ran all nine suites (core 233, exam 147, faults 296, grade 190, gui 123, leak 119, page 165, render 78, shell 186) and the dash gate herself, matching every claimed number. First round where her independent check of my pasted freeze evidence agreed byte-for-byte -- in round 5 she caught me pasting a git status output I had never run. COVERS: BUG-284 (header counter pinned at 31/50), BUG-285 (half-filled Q24 counted as answered on every surface, Chris's find), BUG-286 (earlier save could win; a lost revision race dropped the answer silently), BUG-287 (the exam clock could run BACKWARDS; remaining was one global five handlers wrote), BUG-288 (a test of mine false-failed on correct code ~44% of runs). TWO NON-BLOCKING SUGGESTIONS SHE LEFT OPEN, deliberately not taken in this commit so her PASS would not go stale again: widen 5e's gap from 1.5s to 2s for extra CI headroom, and note that NETFINAL_RENDER_THROTTLE=0 is truthy so it throttles at rate 0 rather than meaning off. She also asked that a durable record say 'no false failures observed in ~45 combined runs' rather than '0 percent', since 0/20 supports an upper bound near 15% by rule of three, and ~45 combined runs tightens it to about 7%. NOT COVERED: no human has sat this exam; auth, Firestore and the callable transport are stubbed in the render suite, so it says nothing about the deployed callables being wired (taskboard 441).
